{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G3iGqyKuSk4Axn8rai83nW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014r6CDpsraiWwtTVcuGYQQZ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research LogUp GKR inner loop","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"I need to understand the fractional sumcheck inner loop in the LogUp GKR phase, specifically the sequential rounds that can't be parallelized. This is in the `crates/cuda-backend/` directory.\n\nSearch for:\n1. The main function `fractional_sumcheck_gpu` in `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n2. How the FoldEval inner rounds work — the compute → D2H → transcript → next round loop\n3. What `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` does and how many times it's called per GKR level\n4. What happens between kernel launches in the sequential loop — is there D2H, CPU work, or other overhead?\n\nKey question: the fractional sumcheck takes ~224ms of kernel time across 141 `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instances + other kernels. Previous attempts to move transcript processing to GPU failed (only 15-25µs CPU work per round). What are the remaining opportunities to speed up this sequential phase?\n\nAlso check: how many GKR levels are there typically, and how many sumcheck rounds per level?\n\nReport in under 400 words. Thoroughness: medium."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":61970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822","uuid":"1bbac926-0a87-4920-832b-e2ad0d614215"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a4e91dfdc2918a0ff","tool_use_id":"toolu_014r6CDpsraiWwtTVcuGYQQZ","description":"Research LogUp GKR inner loop","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"I need to understand the fractional sumcheck inner loop in the LogUp GKR phase, specifically the sequential rounds that can't be parallelized. This is in the `crates/cuda-backend/` directory.\n\nSearch for:\n1. The main function `fractional_sumcheck_gpu` in `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n2. How the FoldEval inner rounds work — the compute → D2H → transcript → next round loop\n3. What `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` does and how many times it's called per GKR level\n4. What happens between kernel launches in the sequential loop — is there D2H, CPU work, or other overhead?\n\nKey question: the fractional sumcheck takes ~224ms of kernel time across 141 `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instances + other kernels. Previous attempts to move transcript processing to GPU failed (only 15-25µs CPU work per round). What are the remaining opportunities to speed up this sequential phase?\n\nAlso check: how many GKR levels are there typically, and how many sumcheck rounds per level?\n\nReport in under 400 words. Thoroughness: medium.","uuid":"b60791bc-996d-42d2-857d-6d6febbd9e8b","session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to understand the fractional sumcheck inner loop in the LogUp GKR phase, specifically the sequential rounds that can't be parallelized. This is in the `crates/cuda-backend/` directory.\n\nSearch for:\n1. The main function `fractional_sumcheck_gpu` in `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n2. How the FoldEval inner rounds work — the compute → D2H → transcript → next round loop\n3. What `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` does and how many times it's called per GKR level\n4. What happens between kernel launches in the sequential loop — is there D2H, CPU work, or other overhead?\n\nKey question: the fractional sumcheck takes ~224ms of kernel time across 141 `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instances + other kernels. Previous attempts to move transcript processing to GPU failed (only 15-25µs CPU work per round). What are the remaining opportunities to speed up this sequential phase?\n\nAlso check: how many GKR levels are there typically, and how many sumcheck rounds per level?\n\nReport in under 400 words. Thoroughness: medium."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014r6CDpsraiWwtTVcuGYQQZ","session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822","uuid":"434cfb67-90a1-46b2-a930-3fe7487c4912","timestamp":"2026-04-14T18:10:34.885Z"}
