The bus term is applied in `LogupMonomialBatch::evaluate()` (line 776), which is called from:\n   - `evaluate_logup_batched()` (line 505-543 in `batch_mle.rs`)\n   - `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval()` (line 1576-onwards in `mod.rs`)\n   - Which is called from the **MLE rounds loop** (line 661 in `mod.rs`)\n\n3. **Measurement context**: The MLE rounds are executed inside the `prover.rap_constraints.mle_rounds` span (line 657-702 in `mod.rs`), which is part of `prover.rap_constraints` - the main measurement scope covering:\n   - Round 0 (constraints/interactions extraction)\n   - LogUp GKR \n   - MLE Rounds\n   - Trace Commit\n\n### Conclusion\n\n**The bus_term_sum contribution is measured within STARK excl trace**, specifically in the MLE Rounds phase (LogUp constraint evaluation). It is NOT part of:\n- Trace generation\n- Preflight execution\n- Metered execution\n\nThe implementation uses a monomial-based batch GPU kernel that efficiently computes and applies the bus term across multiple AIRs in a single launch, contributing to the LogUp zerocheck proof generation."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822","uuid":"606ea17c-a9a1-4c20-9bac-e524c4b96b6b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T18:11:37.461Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand where `apc_apply_bus_kernel` is called and whether it contributes to the \"STARK excl trace\" metric in this prover system. \n\nSearch for:\n1. The definition of `apc_apply_bus_kernel` in the CUDA code under `crates/cuda-backend/`\n2. Where the Rust FFI wrapper for this kernel is called\n3. Whether it's called during trace generation or during constraint evaluation (Round 0, LogUp GKR, etc.)\n\nThe STARK excl trace metric covers: constraints (Round 0, LogUp GKR, MLE Rounds), openings (Stacked Reduction, WHIR), and Trace Commit. It does NOT include trace generation, preflight execution, or metered execution.\n\nReport: which phase calls this kernel, and is it inside STARK exc