{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLGymeib14nKRujS6Pd5LZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-2130-warp-per-trace-mle-eval\n2\t\n3\tMLE Rounds at APC 300 (159ms) scales negatively vs APC 0 (112ms, ratio 0.70x) despite 2.3x fewer cells, because the batch MLE evaluation kernels (`zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel`, `logup_batch_mle_kernel`) assign one full 128-thread block per trace — wasting >75% of threads when `num_y` is small (1–32). At APC 300 with 623 AIR instances (many small APC-generated AIRs), most traces have tiny `num_y`, and the problem worsens each MLE round as `num_y` halves. A warp-per-trace evaluation kernel for small traces (num_y ≤ 32) packs 4 traces into one 128-thread block with warp-level reduction, dramatically reducing block count and improving GPU utilization.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJoRBaETh9cVYr3fnktv3N","session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822","uuid":"e198068b-9745-4b60-8dd2-d1d51551ca98","timestamp":"2026-04-14T21:04:43.798Z"}
