{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RvuuUib899PHMB1N7TL5x2","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-2130-warp-per-trace-mle-monomial\n\nMLE Rounds at APC 300 (159ms) scales negatively vs APC 0 (112ms, ratio 0.70x) despite 2.3x fewer cells. Small APC-generated traces (num_y ≤ 512) are routed to the `zerocheck_monomial_kernel` which parallelizes over monomials with a fixed block size of 256 threads. Since most AIRs have only 5–20 monomials, thread utilization is 2–8%. A warp-per-trace monomial evaluation kernel for traces with few monomials (≤ WARP_SIZE) packs one trace per warp, where each thread handles one y-value and loops over all monomials. This flips the parallelism axis from monomials to y-values, directly producing per-trace sums via warp reduction and eliminating wasted threads.\n\n=== plan.md ===\n# Plan: Warp-per-trace monomial MLE evaluation for small traces\n\n## Goal\n\n=== baseline ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.sqlite\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6086bd80-4e0d-45db-9a25-2370973b0822","uuid":"a5f4849c-0aad-4397-a312-3a5221a3ebbc","timestamp":"2026-04-14T21:21:03.974Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-2130-warp-per-trace-mle-monomial\n\nMLE Rounds at APC 300 (159ms) scales negatively vs APC 0 (112ms, ratio 0.70x) despite 2.3x fewer cells. Small APC-generated traces (num_y ≤ 512) are routed to the `zerocheck_monomial_kernel` which parallelizes over monomials with a fixed block size of 256 threads. Since most AIRs have only 5–20 monomials, thread utilization is 2–8%. A warp-per-trace monomial evaluation kernel for traces with few monomials (≤ WARP_SIZE) packs one trace per warp, where each thread handles one y-value and loops over all monomials. This flips the parallelism axis from monomials to y-values, directly producing per-trace sums via warp reduction and eliminating wasted threads.\n\n=== plan.md ===\n# Plan: Warp-per-trace monomial MLE evaluation for small traces\n\n## Goal\n\n=== baseline ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.sqlite","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
